<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n111484" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φῐλοσόφ-ημα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>,
			τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>a subject of scientific inquiry</i> or <i>a philosophic
				treatise,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν τοῖς ἐγκυκλίοις φ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Cael.</u>
					279a30
				</span></i>
			; of the poems of Homer as allegorized, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				34.4.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in Logic,
				<i>demonstration,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔστι φ. συλλογισμὸς ἀποδεικτικός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Top.</u>
					162a15
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>philosophic principle, rule of conduct,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.1125b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				<u>Anim.Pass.</u>
				1.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>shrewd device</i> or <i>invention,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.269b
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
